# APE fork provenance

Upstream: https://github.com/Attempto/APE
Fork base: 5f4d5354a45fb772763bf1a9543f508f15b28982
Import commit: 7af31add39a430fb5904ecef2f84a4a5b575da69
License: LGPL-3.0-or-later
First-party files: PROVENANCE, prolog/ace_to_pl.pl

The upstream `LICENSE.txt` is retained verbatim in this directory. The four
fields above are machine-read by the `fork-notice` gate in `goal.py check`.

This tree is a liberal in-place fork: upstream files are edited directly,
first-party modules are added directly, and everything outside the compiler's
load and build closure is deleted. Git history against the fork base is the
complete change record. Every upstream file a commit after `Import commit`
touched carries a prominent dated in-file modification notice (GPL-3.0 §5(a)
via LGPL-3.0-or-later); first-party additions state their origin and license
in their file header.

First-party additions:

- `prolog/ace_to_pl.pl` — ACE → plain-Prolog compiler over the APE parser
  (LGPL-3.0-or-later, APE derivative). Sole first-party entry point into this
  tree; contract in its header.

Trust posture: APE runs in separate SWI-Prolog processes over a scratch copy
staged by `tools/goal.py` (`shutil.copytree`, then `vendor/clex/clex_lexicon.pl`
overlaid on the staged demo `prolog/lexicon/clex_lexicon.pl`, then `fit_to_plp`
grammar build); every staged parse — corpus and red probes — reads the full
Clex, so the in-tree demo lexicon is unused at runtime. Python moves bytes
only; DRS interpretation lives entirely in Prolog.
